                    "#Find a base.  The base for your lamp should be sturdy enough to stand on its own, even after you add lamp apparatus and a shade on top.  If you have a hollow base that you need to stabilize, consider partially filling it with something like marbles or sand. Some ideas for lamp bases that you could use:<ref>https://www.justmeasuringup.com/homemade-lamp/</ref>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1 Version 6.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Buy a lamp kit.  These can be found at most hardware stores.  Note that it's possible to purchase the pieces separately, but buying them together will ensure a better fit.  If you do buy the cord separately, choose a #18 size cord.<ref>https://www.apartmenttherapy.com/diy-project-idea-how-to-make-a-lamp-out-of-anything-apartment-therapy-tutorials-189083</ref>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2 Version 6.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Prepare the base for the rod.  The rod is a hollow tube that will run the cord up through the bottom of your base to the lightbulb at the top.  Depending on your base, you may have to drill or cut holes wide enough for the rod at the top and bottom of the lamp.<ref>https://www.rachaelrayshow.com/articles/this-is-how-to-diy-a-lamp-out-of-a-vase</ref>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 3 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Thread the cord through the rod.  The cord should consist of two covered wires stuck together.  Thread it through the rod from bottom to top, leaving 3 or 4 inches (7 to 10 cm) of cord about the base.<ref>http://kennethwingard.com/diy/teapot-lamp/</ref>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Find the hot wire and the neutral wire.  Usually, the neutral wire will be surrounded by ribbed insulation.  If you're unsure, refer to the instructions that came with your lamp kit.<ref>http://hyperphysics.phy-astr.gsu.edu/hbase/electric/hsehld.html</ref>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 12 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*If the wires have two colors at all, the white is the neutral wire and the black is the hot wire.",
                    "#Wrap the wires around the screws on the bulb socket.  The bulb socket in the lamp kit should have two screws of different colors positioned at the base.  Wrap the neutral wire clockwise around the silver (or white) screw, and the hot wire clockwise around the gold (or dark) screw.  If you're unsure, check the manual that came with your lamp kit. Using a screwdriver, tighten the screws down over the wires.<ref>https://designsbystudioc.com/how-to-make-a-lamp-with-a-liquor-bottle-for-the-man-cave/</ref>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 13 Version 4.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Find a base.  The base for your lamp should be sturdy enough to stand on its own, even after you add lamp apparatus and a shade on top.  If you have a hollow base that you need to stabilize, consider partially filling it with something like marbles or sand. Some ideas for lamp bases that you could use:[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1 Version 6.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Buy a lamp kit.  These can be found at most hardware stores.  Note that it's possible to purchase the pieces separately, but buying them together will ensure a better fit.  If you do buy the cord separately, choose a #18 size cord.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2 Version 6.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Prepare the base for the rod.  The rod is a hollow tube that will run the cord up through the bottom of your base to the lightbulb at the top.  Depending on your base, you may have to drill or cut holes wide enough for the rod at the top and bottom of the lamp.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 3 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Thread the cord through the rod.  The cord should consist of two covered wires stuck together.  Thread it through the rod from bottom to top, leaving 3 or 4 inches (7 to 10 cm) of cord about the base.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Find the hot wire and the neutral wire.  Usually, the neutral wire will be surrounded by ribbed insulation.  If you're unsure, refer to the instructions that came with your lamp kit.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 12 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*If the wires have two colors at all, the white is the neutral wire and the black is the hot wire.<ref>http://hyperphysics.phy-astr.gsu.edu/hbase/electric/hsehld.html</ref>",
                    "#Wrap the wires around the screws on the bulb socket.  The bulb socket in the lamp kit should have two screws of different colors positioned at the base.  Wrap the neutral wire clockwise around the silver (or white) screw, and the hot wire clockwise around the gold (or dark) screw.  If you're unsure, check the manual that came with your lamp kit. Using a screwdriver, tighten the screws down over the wires.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 13 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "",
                    "",
                    ""
                ]
            }
        },
