        {
            "id": "21534940",
            "user": "Wikivisual",
            "timestamp": "20:31, 19 December 2016",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(7,835 bytes)",
            "change": 153,
            "summary": "(Saving new step-by-step photos)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Find a base.  The base for your lamp should be sturdy enough to stand on its own, even after you add lamp apparatus and a shade on top.  If you have a hollow base that you need to stabilize, consider partially filling it with something like marbles or sand. Some ideas for lamp bases that you could use:[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Buy a lamp kit.  These can be found at most hardware stores.  Note that it's possible to purchase the pieces separately, but buying them together will ensure a better fit.  If you do buy the cord separately, choose a #18 size cord.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Prepare the base for the rod.  The rod is a hollow tube that will run the cord up through the bottom of your base to the lightbulb at the top.  Depending on your base, you may have to drill or cut holes wide enough for the rod at the top and bottom of the lamp.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 3 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Stabilize the bottom of the base.  Your lamp kit might come with a piece meant to stabilize the bottom of your base.  If it doesn't, simply purchase rubber stoppers.  Affix these at intervals around the base to prevent sliding and lift the base slightly off the table, allowing room for the cord.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 4 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Thread the cord through the rod.  The cord should consist of two covered wires stuck together.  Thread it through the rod from bottom to top, leaving 3 or 4 inches (7 to 10 cm) of cord about the base.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Screw the lock nut onto the end of the lamp rod.  Make sure your cords are threaded to where you want them first.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 6 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Screw the neck onto the lamp rod (optional).  Your lamp kit may or may not come with a flat, broad \"neck\" piece or a rubber stopper to add to the lamp rod.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 7 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Add the harp bottom.  Screw the harp bottom onto the lamp rod, arms facing upward. This will be the base for the rest of the harp.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 8 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Screw on the socket cap.  Put the bowl-shaped socket cap on top of the harp bottom, open end up.  Secure tightly.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 9 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Strip the wires.  Pull the two covered wires at the top of the cord apart, separating about 4 inches (10 cm) down the cord.  Using wire strippers or a knife, remove the insulation from the top 1 inch (2.5 cm) of the cords.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 10 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Tie the wires. Tie the wires into an underwriter's knot, which looks like a pretzel. Doing this will prevent the wires from falling through the rod to the base. To tie an underwriter's knot:[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 11 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Find the hot wire and the neutral wire.  Usually, the neutral wire will be surrounded by ribbed insulation.  If you're unsure, refer to the instructions that came with your lamp kit.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 12 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Wrap the wires around the screws on the bulb socket.  The bulb socket in the lamp kit should have two screws of different colors positioned at the base.  Wrap the neutral wire clockwise around the silver (or white) screw, and the hot wire clockwise around the gold (or dark) screw.  If you're unsure, check the manual that came with your lamp kit. Using a screwdriver, tighten the screws down over the wires.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 13 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Put the socket shell over the bulb socket.  Line it up so that the slot coming up from the bottom of the socket shell aligns with the switch on the bulb socket.  Tuck the cords inside so that they won't be visible, and push down the socket shell until it locks into place.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 14 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Attach the top of the harp.  Squeeze the sides of the harp as you slide them into the slots on the harp bottom.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 15 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Place your lampshade on top of the harp.  Once it's secure, twist down the locknut to secure it.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 16 Version 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Screw a lightbulb into the socket, and plug in your lamp.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 17 Version 4.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Find a base.  The base for your lamp should be sturdy enough to stand on its own, even after you add lamp apparatus and a shade on top.  If you have a hollow base that you need to stabilize, consider partially filling it with something like marbles or sand. Some ideas for lamp bases that you could use:[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Buy a lamp kit.  These can be found at most hardware stores.  Note that it's possible to purchase the pieces separately, but buying them together will ensure a better fit.  If you do buy the cord separately, choose a #18 size cord.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Prepare the base for the rod.  The rod is a hollow tube that will run the cord up through the bottom of your base to the lightbulb at the top.  Depending on your base, you may have to drill or cut holes wide enough for the rod at the top and bottom of the lamp.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 3 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Stabilize the bottom of the base.  Your lamp kit might come with a piece meant to stabilize the bottom of your base.  If it doesn't, simply purchase rubber stoppers.  Affix these at intervals around the base to prevent sliding and lift the base slightly off the table, allowing room for the cord.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 4 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Thread the cord through the rod.  The cord should consist of two covered wires stuck together.  Thread it through the rod from bottom to top, leaving 3 or 4 inches (7 to 10 cm) of cord about the base.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Screw the lock nut onto the end of the lamp rod.  Make sure your cords are threaded to where you want them first.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 6 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Screw the neck onto the lamp rod (optional).  Your lamp kit may or may not come with a flat, broad \"neck\" piece or a rubber stopper to add to the lamp rod.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 7 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Add the harp bottom.  Screw the harp bottom onto the lamp rod, arms facing upward. This will be the base for the rest of the harp.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 8 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Screw on the socket cap.  Put the bowl-shaped socket cap on top of the harp bottom, open end up.  Secure tightly.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 9 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Strip the wires.  Pull the two covered wires at the top of the cord apart, separating about 4 inches (10 cm) down the cord.  Using wire strippers or a knife, remove the insulation from the top 1 inch (2.5 cm) of the cords.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 10 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Tie the wires. Tie the wires into an underwriter's knot, which looks like a pretzel. Doing this will prevent the wires from falling through the rod to the base. To tie an underwriter's knot:",
                    "#Find the hot wire and the neutral wire.  Usually, the neutral wire will be surrounded by ribbed insulation.  If you're unsure, refer to the instructions that came with your lamp kit.",
                    "#Wrap the wires around the screws on the bulb socket.  The bulb socket in the lamp kit should have two screws of different colors positioned at the base.  Wrap the neutral wire clockwise around the silver (or white) screw, and the hot wire clockwise around the gold (or dark) screw.  If you're unsure, check the manual that came with your lamp kit. Using a screwdriver, tighten the screws down over the wires.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 13 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Put the socket shell over the bulb socket.  Line it up so that the slot coming up from the bottom of the socket shell aligns with the switch on the bulb socket.  Tuck the cords inside so that they won't be visible, and push down the socket shell until it locks into place.",
                    "#Attach the top of the harp.  Squeeze the sides of the harp as you slide them into the slots on the harp bottom.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 15 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Place your lampshade on top of the harp.  Once it's secure, twist down the locknut to secure it.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 16 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Screw a lightbulb into the socket, and plug in your lamp.[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 17 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
