            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "{{fa}}Got an odd piece that you want to display, but aren't sure what to do with it? How about making a lamp? You can make lamps out of almost anything, and they provide décor and ambience, in addition to making great conversation pieces. If your crafting self is feeling neglected and you want to spark it back into action, here's a perfect project for you.",
                    "",
                    "[[Category:Lamps and Lampshades]]",
                    "[[Category:Wooden Craft Projects]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "{{fa}}Got an odd piece that you want to display, but aren't sure what to do with it? How about making a lamp? You can make lamps out of almost anything, and they provide décor and ambience, in addition to making great conversation pieces. If your craftsy side is feeling neglected and you want to spark it back into action, here's a perfect project for you.",
                    "[[Category:Candles Lamps and Fireplaces]]"
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "21013892",
            "user": "Votebot",
            "timestamp": "08:31, 24 September 2016",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(7,646 bytes)",
            "change": 0,
            "summary": "(reordering tips and warnings based on votes)",
            "is_minor": true,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "adjustment",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "*Keep in mind that wiring electrical circuits carries some risk.  If the wiring is not correct, you can be shocked or electrocuted or the device can cause a fire.  If you are unsure of what you are doing, you may want to prepare the object you want to make a lamp out of for wiring (the mount, the passageways for the wire, the lamp socket and shade mounting) and let someone more skilled in electrical wiring actually wire up the lamp."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "*Keep in mind that wiring electrical circuits carries some risk.  If the wiring is not correct, you can be shocked or electrocuted or the device can cause a fire.  If you are unsure of what you are doing, you may want to prepare the object you want to make a lamp out of for wiring (the mount, the passageways for the wire, the lamp socket and shade mounting) and let someone more skilled in electrical wiring actually wire up the lamp."
                ]
            }
