        {
            "id": "10619736",
            "user": "Wikiphoto",
            "timestamp": "00:08, 30 July 2013",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(8,971 bytes)",
            "change": 270,
            "summary": "(Enlarging and centering Steps photos)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Find a base.  The base for your lamp should be sturdy enough to stand on its own, even after you add lamp apparatus and a shade on top.  If you have a hollow base that you need to stabilize, consider partially filling it with something like marbles or sand. Some ideas for lamp bases that you could use:<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Wine bottles<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet1.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Log or timber<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Wooden pails or buckets<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet3.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Toys or figurines<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet4.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Hollowed-out books<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet5.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Buy a lamp kit.  These can be found at most hardware stores.  Note that it's possible to purchase the pieces separately, but buying them together will ensure a better fit.  If you do buy the cord separately, choose a #18 size cord.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Detachable harp<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Cord set<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet3.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Push-through socket and socket shell<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet4.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Finial<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet5.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Assorted hardware, like nuts, bolts and washers<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet6.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Prepare the base for the rod.  The rod is a hollow tube that will run the cord up through the bottom of your base to the lightbulb at the top.  Depending on your base, you may have to drill or cut holes wide enough for the rod at the top and bottom of the lamp.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 3.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Stabilize the bottom of the base.  Your lamp kit might come with a piece meant to stabilize the bottom of your base.  If it doesn't, simply purchase rubber stoppers.  Affix these at intervals around the base to prevent sliding and lift the base slightly off the table, allowing room for the cord.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 4.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Thread the cord through the rod.  The cord should consist of two covered wires stuck together.  Thread it through the rod from bottom to top, leaving 3 or 4 inches (7 to 10 cm) of cord about the base.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Before threading, tape the wire ends together so that they fit smoothly inside the rod.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5Bullet1.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*When doing this, make sure that the bottom of the plug doesn't rub against the rod's sharp edge.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5Bullet2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Screw the lock nut onto the end of the lamp rod.  Make sure your cords are threaded to where you want them first.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 6.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Screw the neck onto the lamp rod (optional).  Your lamp kit may or may not come with a flat, broad \"neck\" piece or a rubber stopper to add to the lamp rod.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 7.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Add the harp bottom.  Screw the harp bottom onto the lamp rod, arms facing upward. This will be the base for the rest of the harp.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 8.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Screw on the socket cap.  Put the bowl-shaped socket cap on top of the harp bottom, open end up.  Secure tightly.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 9.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Strip the wires.  Pull the two covered wires at the top of the cord apart, separating about 4 inches (10 cm) down the cord.  Using wire strippers or a knife, remove the insulation from the top 1 inch (2.5 cm) of the cords.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 10.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Tie the wires. Tie the wires into an underwriter's knot, which looks like a pretzel. Doing this will prevent the wires from falling through the rod to the base. To tie an underwriter's knot:<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 11.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Find the hot wire and the neutral wire.  Usually, the neutral wire will be surrounded by ribbed insulation.  If you're unsure, refer to the instructions that came with your lamp kit.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 12.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*If the wires have two colors at all, the white is the neutral wire and the black is the hot wire.<ref>http://hyperphysics.phy-astr.gsu.edu/hbase/electric/hsehld.html</ref><br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 12Bullet1.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Wrap the wires around the screws on the bulb socket.  The bulb socket in the lamp kit should have two screws of different colors positioned at the base.  Wrap the neutral wire clockwise around the silver (or white) screw, and the hot wire clockwise around the gold (or dark) screw.  If you're unsure, check the manual that came with your lamp kit. Using a screwdriver, tighten the screws down over the wires.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 13.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Put the socket shell over the bulb socket.  Line it up so that the slot coming up from the bottom of the socket shell aligns with the switch on the bulb socket.  Tuck the cords inside so that they won't be visible, and push down the socket shell until it locks into place.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 14.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Attach the top of the harp.  Squeeze the sides of the harp as you slide them into the slots on the harp bottom.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 15.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Place your lampshade on top of the harp.  Once it's secure, twist down the locknut to secure it.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 16.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Screw a lightbulb into the socket, and plug in your lamp.<br><br>[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 17.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    ""
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1.jpg|right|300px]]Find a base.  The base for your lamp should be sturdy enough to stand on its own, even after you add lamp apparatus and a shade on top.  If you have a hollow base that you need to stabilize, consider partially filling it with something like marbles or sand. Some ideas for lamp bases that you could use:",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet1.jpg|right|300px]]Wine bottles",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet2.jpg|right|300px]]Log or timber",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet3.jpg|right|300px]]Wooden pails or buckets",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet4.jpg|right|300px]]Toys or figurines",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 1Bullet5.jpg|right|300px]]Hollowed-out books",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2.jpg|right|300px]]Buy a lamp kit.  These can be found at most hardware stores.  Note that it's possible to purchase the pieces separately, but buying them together will ensure a better fit.  If you do buy the cord separately, choose a #18 size cord.",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet2.jpg|right|300px]]Detachable harp",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet3.jpg|right|300px]]Cord set",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet4.jpg|right|300px]]Push-through socket and socket shell",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet5.jpg|right|300px]]Finial",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 2Bullet6.jpg|right|300px]]Assorted hardware, like nuts, bolts and washers",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 3.jpg|right|300px]]Prepare the base for the rod.  The rod is a hollow tube that will run the cord up through the bottom of your base to the lightbulb at the top.  Depending on your base, you may have to drill or cut holes wide enough for the rod at the top and bottom of the lamp.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 4.jpg|right|300px]]Stabilize the bottom of the base.  Your lamp kit might come with a piece meant to stabilize the bottom of your base.  If it doesn't, simply purchase rubber stoppers.  Affix these at intervals around the base to prevent sliding and lift the base slightly off the table, allowing room for the cord.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5.jpg|right|300px]]Thread the cord through the rod.  The cord should consist of two covered wires stuck together.  Thread it through the rod from bottom to top, leaving 3 or 4 inches (7 to 10 cm) of cord about the base.",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5Bullet1.jpg|right|300px]]Before threading, tape the wire ends together so that they fit smoothly inside the rod.",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 5Bullet2.jpg|right|300px]]When doing this, make sure that the bottom of the plug doesn't rub against the rod's sharp edge.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 6.jpg|right|300px]]Screw the lock nut onto the end of the lamp rod.  Make sure your cords are threaded to where you want them first.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 7.jpg|right|300px]]Screw the neck onto the lamp rod (optional).  Your lamp kit may or may not come with a flat, broad \"neck\" piece or a rubber stopper to add to the lamp rod.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 8.jpg|right|300px]]Add the harp bottom.  Screw the harp bottom onto the lamp rod, arms facing upward. This will be the base for the rest of the harp.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 9.jpg|right|300px]]Screw on the socket cap.  Put the bowl-shaped socket cap on top of the harp bottom, open end up.  Secure tightly.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 10.jpg|right|300px]]Strip the wires.  Pull the two covered wires at the top of the cord apart, separating about 4 inches (10 cm) down the cord.  Using wire strippers or a knife, remove the insulation from the top 1 inch (2.5 cm) of the cords.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 11.jpg|right|300px]]Tie the wires. Tie the wires into an underwriter's knot, which looks like a pretzel. Doing this will prevent the wires from falling through the rod to the base. To tie an underwriter's knot:",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 12.jpg|right|300px]]Find the hot wire and the neutral wire.  Usually, the neutral wire will be surrounded by ribbed insulation.  If you're unsure, refer to the instructions that came with your lamp kit.",
                    "#*[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 12Bullet1.jpg|right|300px]]If the wires have two colors at all, the white is the neutral wire and the black is the hot wire.<ref>http://hyperphysics.phy-astr.gsu.edu/hbase/electric/hsehld.html</ref>",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 13.jpg|right|300px]]Wrap the wires around the screws on the bulb socket.  The bulb socket in the lamp kit should have two screws of different colors positioned at the base.  Wrap the neutral wire clockwise around the silver (or white) screw, and the hot wire clockwise around the gold (or dark) screw.  If you're unsure, check the manual that came with your lamp kit. Using a screwdriver, tighten the screws down over the wires.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 14.jpg|right|300px]]Put the socket shell over the bulb socket.  Line it up so that the slot coming up from the bottom of the socket shell aligns with the switch on the bulb socket.  Tuck the cords inside so that they won't be visible, and push down the socket shell until it locks into place.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 15.jpg|right|300px]]Attach the top of the harp.  Squeeze the sides of the harp as you slide them into the slots on the harp bottom.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 16.jpg|right|300px]]Place your lampshade on top of the harp.  Once it's secure, twist down the locknut to secure it.",
                    "#[[Image:Build a Lamp Step 17.jpg|right|300px]]Screw a lightbulb into the socket, and plug in your lamp."
                ]
            }
        },
